WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.910
I told our school agent: remind me

2
00:00:02.910 --> 00:00:04.270
about the thing next week.

3
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:07.310
It answered with three questions.

4
00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:11.360
Which thing, which day, what time?

5
00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:13.020
Fair enough, really.

6
00:00:14.330 --> 00:00:16.950
Today: how to ask an agent clearly.

7
00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:20.930
An agent can only act on what you write.

8
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:24.450
When a detail is missing, a good agent

9
00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.410
asks, like Darsi Tiny asking which

10
00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:27.730
village.

11
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:30.980
A weaker one guesses, and a

12
00:00:30.980 --> 00:00:31.840
guess can be wrong.

13
00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.190
A clear request has four parts.

14
00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:37.640
The goal, what you want done.

15
00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:42.320
The details: who, what, when and where.

16
00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:45.360
The limits, what it must not do.

17
00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.630
And what done looks like,

18
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:48.790
so you can check it.

19
00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.850
A vague one: tell the

20
00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:53.290
parents about the trip.

21
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:56.900
A clear one: draft a message to six B’s

22
00:00:56.900 --> 00:00:59.340
parents saying Friday’s farm trip is

23
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.560
cancelled, and show me before sending.

24
00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:05.110
The clear one has a goal, details,

25
00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:07.750
a limit and a finish line.

26
00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.710
It’s like the note you leave for a

27
00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:13.690
supply teacher: which page, who needs

28
00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:16.090
help, and what not to start yet.

29
00:01:16.730 --> 00:01:19.350
An agent needs that note every time.

30
00:01:20.030 --> 00:01:21.250
It can’t read your mind.

31
00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:23.740
Limits matter most.

32
00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:27.280
Words like don’t send it yet tell

33
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:28.360
the agent where to stop.

34
00:01:28.990 --> 00:01:31.030
But a limit in words is a

35
00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.590
request, not a lock.

36
00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:35.400
A good app backs it up by

37
00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:37.180
asking you before any action.

38
00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:39.030
Quick check!

39
00:01:39.820 --> 00:01:42.140
Which of these requests will an

40
00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:43.980
agent get right the first time?

41
00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:46.070
The Monday one.

42
00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.700
It has the goal, a reminder, and

43
00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:52.460
every detail: the day, the time,

44
00:01:53.020 --> 00:01:54.660
the class and the subject.

45
00:01:55.370 --> 00:01:58.210
There’s nothing left to guess or to ask.

46
00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:01.220
And afterwards, it’s easy to check.

47
00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:03.720
Wording matters too.

48
00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:06.680
With wordings it learned, Darsi Tiny

49
00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:09.320
gets the tool and every detail right

50
00:02:09.320 --> 00:02:12.040
nearly every time; with new wordings,

51
00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.720
about four times in five.

52
00:02:14.380 --> 00:02:17.620
Plain, complete requests help every agent.

53
00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:21.950
In the app, build a request from parts: a

54
00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:25.470
role, a task, the context and a format.

55
00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:29.170
Ask with two parts, then add the context

56
00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.570
and watch the answer fit your class.

57
00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:33.460
Your turn.

58
00:02:34.070 --> 00:02:36.270
I asked: what’s the weather tomorrow.

59
00:02:36.930 --> 00:02:38.630
What will a good agent do?

60
00:02:39.860 --> 00:02:41.700
It asks which village,

61
00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.800
because a detail is missing.

62
00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:47.240
Remember: a clear request has a goal,

63
00:02:47.720 --> 00:02:51.140
details, limits and what done looks like.

64
00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:53.000
Missing details make an

65
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.980
agent ask, or guess.

66
00:02:55.770 --> 00:02:58.110
And a limit in words should be

67
00:02:58.110 --> 00:02:59.110
backed up by the app.

68
00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:01.710
Try it in class tomorrow:

69
00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:03.930
play Vague to clear.

70
00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.300
Pairs write a vague request, then

71
00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:09.960
rewrite it with a goal, details,

72
00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.160
limits and a finish line.

73
00:03:12.740 --> 00:03:14.840
A partner plays the agent and

74
00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:16.460
does only what is written.

75
00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:19.390
Where did the agent have to guess?
